7. Compositor: reel/showcase/index.html plus src/ (main.js, edit.js, camera.js, stage.js, type.js), run in headless Chromium and deterministic. A pure pose(t) returns:
- the camera (framing solver, keyed moves, three cuts, drift, lean with 2400 px perspective);
- the two recorded frames each device's screen cross-fades between (with holds);
- the cursor and touch marks from the meta logs;
- the URL pill text, and the status-bar fill and glyph colour;
- the overlays (screen-space DOM in General Sans and Cabinet Grotesk loaded from app/fonts) and the two chips.
Device frames and shadows are SVG or DOM. Screens come from take frames pre-scaled with Lanczos3 (sharp), in two mip levels. The Linen stage gets the Paper falloff. Motion blur is a 180° shutter, ±1/120 s around each output frame. While anything moves it takes 9 taps with triangular weights, for camera and site motion alike, and the screens cross-fade between their recorded frames. A single sample applies at rest, or when a click or tap switches the page's state inside the shutter. Before F(128) the desktop shows D1 at the frame's own time, so the hero film's 24 fps frames never double-expose. No tap reaches across a cut. Frame 0 is bare Linen. Then σ 1.2/255 dither is added.
